-- title:
--   Clearing poles on a strict second-kind residue disc
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a positive integer $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, together with modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr` and integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ for the two degeneracy maps `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` from level $N$ to level $Nq$. Let $P$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` for these data, assume $q \nmid N$ and that $\mathrm{red}(c) = 0$ holds exactly for $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $Q$ be a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-function field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` which is strict of the second kind for $P$, that is $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,Q$ equals the geometric Frobenius image of $\bar v := P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,Q$ while the twofold Frobenius image of $\bar v$ differs from $\bar v$. Assume furthermore: some pair $c \in k \times k$ is a centre of $\bar v$, in the sense that $\bar v$ gives positive order to $\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,N - c_1$ and to $\mathrm{jNGeomGen}\,k\,N - c_2$, and $\bar v$ is the only place of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` with that centre; and the values $\bar v(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$, $\bar v(\mathrm{jNGeomGen})$ are each moved by the $q^2$-power map. Let $z, y_1, y_2$ be elements of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, $u \in A$ and $w : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to A$ such that $(z; y_1, y_2)$ is a second-kind triple at $\bar v$ with value $\mathrm{red}(u)$, i.e. either $z = \mathrm{jQFun}$, $y_1 = \mathrm{jNQFun}$, $y_2 = \mathrm{jFun}$ and $\bar v$ gives order exactly $1$ to $\mathrm{jGeomGen} - \mathrm{red}(u)$, or $z = \mathrm{jNQFun}$, $y_1 = \mathrm{jQFun}$, $y_2 = \mathrm{jFun}$ and $\bar v$ gives order exactly $1$ to $\mathrm{jNGeomGen} - \mathrm{red}(u)$; and such that $Q$ gives positive order to $z - u$ and to $(![y_1,y_2])_j - w_j$ for both $j$. Finally let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` lying in the valuation subring of every place $W$ that is strict of the second kind for $P$ and satisfies $P.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,W = \bar v$. Then there is a polynomial $H$ in three variables indexed by `Option (Fin 2)` with coefficients in $A$ such that $\mathrm{red}$ of the value of $H$ at $(u; w_0, w_1)$ is nonzero, and such that $f$ times the value of $H$ at $(z; y_1, y_2)$, coefficients being mapped into the function field through $A \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by $\mathrm{jFun}\,N\,q$.
--
--   This is the horizontal pole-clearing step at a smooth point: a function regular at all strict second-kind places above a given reduced place $\bar v$ can be multiplied by a polynomial in the coordinate triple, chosen to be a unit at $\bar v$, so as to become integral over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j]$, i.e. to have poles only where $j$ does. It feeds the construction of models for the second-kind local rings, being cited by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.IsModel.exists_evalBar_eq_mul_evalBar_of_mem_smoothLocalRingSnd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.IsModel.exists_evalBar_eq_mul_evalBar_of_mem_smoothLocalRingSnd).
